<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<robot name="hypernova_go2_proxy">
  <!--
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
Derived from Unitree Robotics unitree_ros, commit 38a9b00ecbff0b70e85a7627eb9c65db9a2341f7.
Original copyright and full terms in LICENSE.unitree. Changes: HYPERNOVA contributors, 2026-10-30.
DESIGN / ASSUMPTION LEDGER (canonical XML; not generated at runtime):
Consumer: URDF viewers and Isaac Sim import; provisional simulation surrogate, not hardware control.
SI units m, kg, s, rad; body +X forward, +Y left, +Z up. DAE source metres; converted STL metres, scale 1.
Original physical links, link frames, geometry origins, joint origins, axes, angle limits,
COM and inertia tensors are retained numerically. Source is vendor URDF, not measured HYPERNOVA CAD.
All original mesh visuals use meshes/<original-name>.stl; collision primitives retain source poses.
Each existing link/joint's XML is its per-element ledger of source dimensions/frames/inertials.
Hip positive motion follows right-hand rotation around local +X; thigh/calf around local +Y.
FL/FR/RL/RR mean front-left/front-right/rear-left/rear-right. Zero pose is vendor kinematic zero,
NOT a valid standing configuration (knees must be flexed inside their negative angle limits).
Original 12 fixed *_rotor links remain vendor inertials, NOT reflected actuator armature.
imu, radar, front_camera are frame-only: zero inertials removed. Fixed calf collision helper
links are massless shapes whose mass is already represented in the parent calf inertial.
Original total mass 16.087 kg and dimensions retained at user's revised request; no scaling.
GO-M8010-6: hip/thigh output maxima 23.7 Nm, 30 rad/s at 24 V. Knee external ratio 1.5:
ideal output maxima 35.55 Nm, 20 rad/s. Internal 6.33 ratio already included, not applied twice.
Latest HW decision used over older all-joint 23.7/30 task note. Efficiency, continuous torque,
torque-speed envelope, motor inertia, friction/damping and actual masses unverified; not invented.
Top equipment_payload: fixed to base, x/y aligned with BASE COM projection, z=0.14 m assumed.
It is not the pose-dependent whole-robot COM. Assumed uniform .24 x .14 x .08 m box, 2.5 kg.
Its principal moments computed as m*(b*b+c*c)/12, inertial frame = centered box frame.
front_lidar: fixed base-relative (.35,0,.04) m, identity rotation; assumed .06 x .10 x .06 m housing.
Its mass is INCLUDED in the dorsal 2.5 kg lump, NOT counted a second time; this approximates
actual equipment COM/inertia by a dorsal box. Total 18.587 kg. Actual mounting dimensions unknown.
LiDAR optical frame +X boresight: azimuth [-60,60] deg, elevation [-17.5,17.5] deg.
URDF represents housing/frame only; config/front_lidar.json and companion Isaac helper define RTX rays.
Preserve front_lidar fixed frame on import (disable fixed-joint merge); no original radar is activated.
Retained vendor inertials can disagree with simplified collision-box inertia estimates.
Repeated material children cleaned; DAE scene transforms baked to STL without decimation; embedded colors replaced by URDF material.
-->
